  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Consider the string of infinite length obtained by repeating `abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz` infinitely many times. That is, it looks like `abc...xyzabc...xyzabc...`\n\nLet string BBB be the prefix of this string of length MMM. For example,\n\n\nif M=6M = 6M=6, B=B =B= `abcdef`\nif M=29M = 29M=29, B=B = B= `abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabc`\nVedansh calls a string XXX special if it contains BBB as a substring. Formally, XXX is special if for some 1≤L≤R≤∣X∣1 \\le L \\le R \\le |X|1≤L≤R≤∣X∣, XL…R=BX_{L\\ldots R} = BXL…R​=B.\n\nVedansh has string SSS of length NNN (consisting of lowercase Latin letters only). He wants to convert SSS into a special string. To do so he can perform the following operation:\n\n\nPick an iii such that 1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N and delete SiS_iSi​. The remaining parts of SSS are concatenated.\nSince Vedansh is lazy, he wants to do this in the **minimum** number of operations or determine if SSS cannot be converted to a special string. Help Vedansh in doing so.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains a single integer TTT — the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nEach test case consists of three lines of input\n\nThe first line of each test case contains an integer NNN — the length of the string SSS.\nThe second line of each test case contains the string SSS which consists of lowercase Latin letters only.\nThe third line of each test case contains an integer MMM — the length of the string BBB whose form is described in the statement.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, if AAA can be converted to a special string, output the **minimum** number of operations to do so. Otherwise output −1-1−1.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤10001 \\leq T \\leq 10001≤T≤1000",
      "1≤M≤N≤1061 \\leq M \\leq N \\leq 10^61≤M≤N≤106",
      "SSS consists of only lowercase Latin letters",
      "It is guaranteed that the sum of NNN over all test case does not exceed 10610^6106.",
      "Subtasks"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
