        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n9\nababbdced\n4\n7\nbdcgehx\n5\n6\nacbcbd\n3",
        "output": "3\n-1\n1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: M=4M = 4M=4, so B=abcdB = abcdB=abcd. We can delete the following characters from SSS:\nababbdcedabab{\\color{red}bd}c{\\color{red}e}dababbdced →\\rightarrow→ ababcd‾ab\\underline{abcd}ababcd​, which has BBB as a substring.\nTest case 222: M=5M = 5M=5, so B=abcdeB = abcdeB=abcde. It can be shown that SSS can not be converted into a special string.\nTest case 333: M=3M = 3M=3, so B=abcB = abcB=abc. We can delete the following characters from SSS:\nacbcbda{\\color{red}c}bcbdacbcbd →\\rightarrow→ abc‾bd\\underline{abc}bdabc​bd, which has BBB as a substring."
      }
